-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Pop de Australia y Nueva Zelanda","scene_id":128062745971935,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#antipodes-pop","chapters":["Sección 5.11"],"pages":[[1,159,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":159,"text":"…had finally become a regular band) adopted a more traditional format. Clean's guitarist Peter Gutteridge helped vocalist Martin Phillips form the Chills (1), whose Kaleidoscope World (1982), Rolling Moon (1982), Pink Frost (1984) and the EP Lost (1985) sprinkled cliches of folk-rock, psychedelia, garage rhythm'n'blues and Mersey-beat over naive lullabies. Several years later, a new line-up assembled by Phillips recorded the best Chills album, Submarine Bells (1990), more overtly inspired by the Beach Boys and Big Star, the first step towards the conversion to the mainstream that…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":234,"text":"…of their phantasmagoric orchestrations. Luna (1), formed by Galaxie 500's guitarist and vocalist Dean Wareham, Feelies' drummer Stanley Demeski and Chills' bassist Justin Harwood, specialized in shy, tender, whispered/conversational pop tunes, best on Bewitched (1994). Minneapolis' Motion Picture (1)…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":120713450438284,"type":"album","name":"Brave Words","list_id":139102853169805,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Dunedin Sound","src":"musthear","rank":3,"year":1900,"note":null,"yt":"GzKPDyhXSN8","scaruffi":null},{"id":120713450438284,"type":"album","name":"Brave Words","list_id":161051722508702,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","src":"musthear","rank":84,"year":1900,"note":null,"yt":"GzKPDyhXSN8","scaruffi":null},{"id":211029835847485,"type":"album","name":"Submarine Bells","list_id":150689015758751,"list":"Genres only music snobs know about @LadoB","src":"musthear","rank":29,